      "side": 1,
      "message": "From this file, the logic behind `pending_close_bda` is \n\n1. After `bta_dm_gatt_disc_complete`, we schedule a 1 second timer `gatt_close_timer` to close the discovery GATT client when no one else is using it. This assigns `pending_close_bda` to the current `peer_bdaddr`\n\nThen two things could happen:\n\n2.1 When `gatt_close_timer` pops, it closes the discovery GATT client in `gatt_close_timer_cb` and it clears `pending_close_bda` when the close API is called\n\n2.2. When someone calls `btm_dm_start_gatt_discovery`, it checks if the discovering device address is the same as `pending_close_bda`, if so, cancel `gatt_close_timer_cb` and clear `pending_close_bda` so that we do not create a duplicate GATT client for the same device. \n\nWith your CL change\n\n1. `gatt_close_timer` is scheduled for a particular GATT client, with a `conn_id`\n\n2.1 When `gatt_close_timer` pops, it closes the discovery GATT client in `gatt_close_timer_cb` with the `conn_id` and it clears `pending_close_bda` when the close API is called\n\n2.2. When someone calls `btm_dm_start_gatt_discovery`, it checks if the discovering device address is the same as `pending_close_bda`, if so, cancel `gatt_close_timer_cb` and clear `pending_close_bda` so that we do not create a duplicate GATT client for the same device. \n\nThere is an implicit association with the closing `conn_id` and `pending_close_bda` and `gatt_close_timer` can only be scheduled once. If `gatt_close_timer` is scheduled twice for another `conn_id` with a different MAC address, we have a bug. However this is highly unlikely because only one GATT service discovery could happen at a time and for two to complete within 1 second, the chance is very low. \n\nAnd hence I think the logic is indeed correct since `pending_close_bda` is only tracking the `gatt_close_timer`, but this is very ugly. \n\nWhen makes it look a bit nicer is to add a \n- pending_close_conn_id\nAnd do not pass conn_id as a field in the timer since we assume the timer can only be scheduled once. \n\nThen before setting `gatt_close_timer` or calling `bta_dm_close_gatt_conn`, we always set `pending_close_conn_id` to `bta_dm_discovery_cb.conn_id`",
